{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Let them praise the name of YHWH, for His name alone is exalted</b> — that it not perish, as all these will perish and the particulars will vanish." "And the meaning of <b>for His name alone is exalted</b> — that He is the guardian of the universals. And behold, he stated that all created beings in the lower world will perish; only Israel alone will not. Therefore he said: <b>and He will raise a horn for His people; praise for all His devout ones</b> — that in this matter the devout of Israel will be praised, who are the devout of HaShem, not all Israel."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 148, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:08.344507711Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}